stats.text:
A condition is a temporary game state. The definition of a condition says how it affects its recipient, and various rules define how to end a condition. This glossary defines these conditions:

- {ref:condition/blinded}
- {ref:condition/charmed}
- {ref:condition/deafened}
- {ref:condition/exhaustion}
- {ref:condition/frightened}
- {ref:condition/grappled}
- {ref:condition/incapacitated}
- {ref:condition/invisible}
- {ref:condition/paralyzed}
- {ref:condition/petrified}
- {ref:condition/poisoned}
- {ref:condition/prone}
- {ref:condition/restrained}
- {ref:condition/stunned}
- {ref:condition/unconscious}

A condition doesn't stack with itself; a recipient either has a condition or doesn't. The {ref:condition/exhaustion} condition is an exception to that rule.
